        "parms": "1. A patchbay into router. Each column is one of router's inputs and each row one of its outputs. Click the bottom left cell, column 0 and row 1, then click 100: it reaches the right box. The list box shows the click as <column> <row> <value>, the message router reads.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 46": {
        "ID": 46,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "270.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. One input can reach both outputs, and both inputs can share one. On the engine Phi ships, a cell's value comes out as a decimal, 1., and router only takes whole numbers, so pack 0 0 0 rounds the list first (#522).",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 47": {
        "ID": 47,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "420.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "3. A 16-step pattern on four rows: each column is a step, each row a sound. Click cells to place hits, then turn on the toggle to play the pattern on the master bus.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 48": {
        "ID": 48,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "520.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "4. metro steps counter and % 16 through the columns, and prepend getcolumn asks the grid for one column at a time. The answer, one value per row, leaves the right outlet: the second list box shows it. getrow asks for a row.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 49": {
        "ID": 49,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "650.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "5. unpack spreads the column over four voices, the top row on the left. sel 1 bangs for a cell that is on, pack 1 0 0 150 sends line a short envelope, and ~* plays it on the voice.",
        "type": ".text"
